    "updated_at": "2017-02-08T02:42:12Z",
    "body": "I just re-reviewed the introductory sections of each concept and they seem to be pretty distinct. E.g. maplike explains that it's something you apply to interfaces and causes them to get certain methods, whereas record explains that it's a type that represents string-keyed mappings and is represented in JS by a plain object. What concretely is missing that might emphasize these things better? What concrete phrases make them seem similar, despite the differences the rest of the surrounding paragraphs are clear about calling out?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
